Map data (the World atlas, App/Fernlet/World/Atlas/WorldAtlas.pack)

The atlas is built on the build machine by Scripts/world-atlas/ and ships
inside the app; the app never downloads map data.

Land, minor islands, marine areas, countries, populated places and urban
areas: Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), 1:10m, in the
public domain. No credit is required; Fernlet gives it anyway.

Climate zones: Beck, H. E., Zimmermann, N. E., McVicar, T. R., Vergopolan,
N., Berg, A., & Wood, E. F. (2018). Present and future Koppen-Geiger
climate classification maps at 1-km resolution. Scientific Data, 5,
180214. https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2018.214. Licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Fernlet changed the data:
the present-day 0.083-degree map was reduced to 0.1-degree cells (the
majority class of each) and its classes turned into terrain.
